Third-party software in the Docker image
----------------------------------------

The FemtoShare Docker image includes FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), which
FemtoShare runs as a separate program to convert uploaded videos. The image
installs FFmpeg from Alpine Linux's "ffmpeg" package. That build is licensed
under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later because it enables
GPL components such as libx264 and libx265. It does not include any
"nonfree" components; AAC audio is encoded with FFmpeg's built-in encoder.

The source code for that FFmpeg build, including Alpine's build recipe and
patches, is available from Alpine Linux:

  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.22-stable/community/ffmpeg
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/

Other Alpine packages in the image are distributed under their own licenses,
which you can list from inside the container with "apk info --license".

H.264 and AAC are covered by patents in some countries. This notice is not
legal advice about patent licensing.
